    'nuances' => array(
        'ON AN ENQUIRY/CONTACT CARD, KEEP THE INVITATION SPEECH ACT. English „Ask how X can help you…” is „Zapraszamy do kontaktu, aby dowiedzieć się, jak…”. The bare declarative „Dowiedzą się Państwo, jak…” asserts an outcome the visitor has not yet obtained and turns a CTA into a statement; reserve it for descriptive prose, and never use the literal „Prosimy zapytać, jak…”. (This refines the pack\'s existing Ask-how note, which currently licenses only the declarative.)',
        'A FORM FIELD LABEL THAT SITS ABOVE A CONTROL IS A BARE POLISH NOUN PHRASE, NEVER „Prosimy + bezokolicznik”: „Select your support team” is „Zespół wsparcia”, „Choose a topic” is „Temat”, „Select your country” is „Kraj”. A polite request in the label beside a bare-imperative placeholder („Wybierz opcję”) puts two registers in one glance. Keep „Prosimy…” only for full instruction sentences in prose. (This overrides the pack\'s own „Prosimy wybrać zespół wsparcia” example.)',
        'A BACK, SKIP OR RESET LINK INSIDE A FORM IS A CONTROL AND TAKES THE BARE IMPERATIVE: „← Choose a different topic” is „← Wybierz inny temat”, „Start over” is „Zacznij od nowa”. Anything the buyer clicks to move through the form follows the button rule, not the prose rule.',
        'A BRAND LOCKUP IS TRANSLATED IDENTICALLY — OR NOT AT ALL — IN EVERY SURFACE IT APPEARS IN, INCLUDING alt, aria-label, title AND <title>. If „Ascential Test & Measurement” stays English in the aria-label and the page title, the alt text must not become „Ascential Systemy kontrolno-pomiarowe”. Decide once per lockup and apply it to visible copy and attributes alike; a screen-reader-only string that disagrees with the visible one is still an inconsistency.',
        '„connected” DESCRIBING A MONITORING, TELEMETRY OR IoT PLATFORM MEANS NETWORK-CONNECTED, NOT INTEGRATED: „This connected, performance management solution” is „To połączone w sieć rozwiązanie do zarządzania wydajnością”. „zintegrowane” means the modules are integrated with one another — a different product claim. (This supersedes the pack line mapping „connected solution” → „zintegrowane rozwiązanie”.) Reserve „zintegrowany” for English „integrated”.',
        '„zagrożenie” TAKES THE GENITIVE OF WHAT IS THREATENED, NOT „dla” + THE ABSTRACT NOUN IT ALREADY CONTAINS: „immediate safety risk” is „bezpośrednie zagrożenie bezpieczeństwa”, not „zagrożenie dla bezpieczeństwa” (a threat to safety-in-general — tautological). Keep „zagrożenie dla środowiska” where the object really is a separate entity. Apply the same de-pleonasm test to „ryzyko ryzyka”-shaped pairs such as „ryzyko zagrożenia”.',
        'USE ONE YES/NO QUESTION PATTERN ACROSS THE SITE, AND IN THE FORMAL Państwo REGISTER THAT PATTERN IS „Czy …?”: „Czy potrzebują Państwo wsparcia już teraz?”, „Czy szukają Państwo …?”, „Czy mogą Państwo podać …?”. An intonation question without „Czy” is grammatical but reads as a dropped word next to siblings that keep it; never mix the two patterns on one page.',
        'ONE POLISH NAME PER BUSINESS SEGMENT, AND EXACTLY TWO FORMS FOR AEROSPACE — NO THIRD VARIANT. The division „Aerospace & industrials” is „Lotnictwo i przemysł” in nav, footer and headings; the narrower brand-scope option „Bauer | Aerospace” is „Bauer | Lotnictwo” so the two dropdown options stay distinguishable. Never emit „Lotnictwo i kosmonautyka” as a third rendering; delete any pack example that licenses it.',
        'ONE POLISH LABEL PER UI CONCEPT WITHIN A SINGLE COMPONENT, CHECKED ACROSS THE WHOLE COMPONENT, NOT PER SEGMENT. A heading and the sentence under it, a field label and its own control, a warning and its own instruction must reuse the identical Polish noun phrase: „Wymagana weryfikacja zabezpieczeń:” with „Prosimy ukończyć powyższą weryfikację zabezpieczeń…”. Two synonyms for one on-screen object two lines apart is a defect even when both are correct Polish.',
        'A COUNTER OR STAT LABEL MUST BE TRUE OF A PLURAL. Before keeping a literal modifier in a „<number>+ <label>” counter, test whether the noun can exist in that quantity: a company has exactly one „kraj macierzysty”, so „20+ krajów macierzystych” is self-contradictory — write „20+ krajów, w których działamy”. Keep the genitive plural, but render the sense of the English modifier („home” = where the company is present), never its dictionary word, when the literal word collides with the number.',
        'DO NOT UPGRADE AN ENGLISH ASSURANCE VERB INTO A POLISH WARRANTY VERB. „ensures / guarantees that…” in marketing prose is „zapewnia, że…”; „gwarantuje” is contract-and-warranty language in Polish commercial usage and creates a legal claim the English does not make. Reserve „gwarancja/gwarantować” for an actual stated warranty.',
        'RENDER A PURPOSE-AND-OUTCOME PARTICIPLE, NOT AN INTENTION, WHEN THE ENGLISH ASSERTS A RESULT. „…designed for aerospace and automotive industries, ensuring safety, reliability, and performance excellence” is „…zapewniające bezpieczeństwo, niezawodność i najwyższą wydajność”; „z myślą o bezpieczeństwie…” downgrades a stated outcome to an intention. This applies to meta descriptions, og: tags and JSON-LD, which are the first Polish a buyer reads.',
        'TRACE AN AMBIGUOUS POLISH PRONOUN OR ELIDED SUBJECT AND NAME THE NOUN WHEN TWO CANDIDATES SHARE GENDER. English „it” is unambiguous; Polish „będzie bezpieczny” after two masculine nouns („produkt”, „ktoś”) is not — write „…ufa, że produkt ten będzie bezpieczny…”. Whenever an adjective or verb could attach to a person as easily as to the thing, repeat the head noun or add „ten/ta/to”.',
        'A PRODUCT-CATEGORY LABEL NAMES THE INDUSTRY, NOT THE PHYSICAL ACT. „refrigeration” in a product or capability list is „chłodnictwo” (the field); „chłodzenie” is the act of cooling and belongs in a process description such as „chłodzenie w cyklu sprężania pary”. Apply the same test to „machining”, „welding”, „balancing”: pick the trade-sector noun in a catalogue list and the process noun in a sentence about what a machine does.',
        'aria-label AND alt TEXT ARE SENTENCES AND MUST PARSE, NOT BE WORD-STACKS. Attach each modifier to the noun it modifies in English: „Privacy opt-out controls” is „Ustawienia rezygnacji – prywatność”, not „Kontrola rezygnacji z prywatności” (which reads „control of opting out of privacy”); „Mobile primary” (a nav landmark) is „Główna nawigacja mobilna”, not „Mobilna wersja główna”. Name the UI object the label actually points at before translating.',
        'KEEP THE COMBATIVE BRAND VERB. „tackles the most challenging problems” is „mierzy się z najtrudniejszymi problemami”, not „zajmuje się…” (deals with/handles), which flattens the posture behind „Impossible? Done.”. Same test for „we engineer new possibilities” → „opracowujemy nowe możliwości” (never the neutral „tworzymy”, and never „projektujemy możliwości”): when English picks an effortful verb, the Polish must be equally effortful.',
        '„actionable” IN AN ANALYTICS CLAIM IS NOT „praktyczny”. Write „informacje gotowe do wykorzystania” or „konkretne wskazówki do działania” — „praktyczne informacje” means merely useful and removes the immediacy that sells a monitoring platform. Distinguish it from „timely insights” („wnioski we właściwym czasie”), which is a different promise again.',
        'RENDER EVERY DATE IN ONE STRIP OR LIST WITH ONE POLISH FORMAT, AND ALWAYS SPELL THE MONTH IN LONG-FORM CARD DATES: „22 września 2026”, „14 września 2026”, „8 września 2026”. Never mix a long-form month with an abbreviation inside sibling cards; if an abbreviated Polish month is ever unavoidable, it takes a period („14 wrz. 2026”), never bare „wrz”.',
        'THE SITE\'S DECIDED REGISTER SPLIT IS DELIBERATE AND MUST NOT BE FLIPPED BACK AND FORTH: Państwo in all prose, questions, form instructions and field labels; the bare imperative on the control itself („Utwórz zgłoszenie serwisowe”, „Zamów demo”, „Wybierz opcję”, „Czytaj artykuł →”). Do not convert CTAs to „Prosimy…” or to nominal phrases, and do not drop prose into ty-forms to match a button. Hold this pairing across every page so the same English control always yields the same Polish control.',
        'NON-SPATIAL ENGLISH „where” IS NEVER „gdzie” AFTER AN ABSTRACT NOUN. „problems where the cost of failure is high” is „problemy, w przypadku których koszt awarii jest wysoki”; „issues, where the machine is down” is „problemy, gdy maszyna jest unieruchomiona”.',
        'For a CAPTCHA or bot check, „security verification” is „weryfikacja zabezpieczeń”, never „weryfikacja bezpieczeństwa” — in a heavy-industry context the latter reads as a safety audit. And English positional „above/below” after a noun phrase becomes an attributive adjective BEFORE the noun in Polish: „Prosimy ukończyć powyższą weryfikację zabezpieczeń”, never „…weryfikację zabezpieczeń powyżej”.',
        'NEVER OPEN A POLISH SENTENCE WITH „Lub” OR „Albo” TO MIRROR ENGLISH „Or …”. This supersedes the older pack note that licensed „Lub gdy…”: write „Dotyczy to również sytuacji, w których…”, „Obejmuje to także przypadki, gdy…”, or fold the clause into the preceding sentence with a comma. English starts sentences with coordinating conjunctions; formal Polish does not.',
        'ENGLISH „Ask how X can help you…” IS AN INVITATION TO LEARN, NOT AN INSTRUCTION TO ASK. Render it „Dowiedzą się Państwo, jak…” or „Zapraszamy do kontaktu, aby dowiedzieć się, jak…” — never the literal „Prosimy zapytać, jak…”, which tells the buyer to perform an act of asking and reads as a traced card description.',
        'THE DEFAULT OPTION OF A <select> AND ANY TEXT INSIDE A CONTROL TAKES THE SHORT BARE IMPERATIVE, NOT „Prosimy + bezokolicznik”. „Select an option” is „Wybierz opcję” or „— wybierz —”, never „Prosimy wybrać opcję”: a five-syllable polite request inside a dropdown is not a pattern Polish users see. Keep „Prosimy…” for full form instructions in prose.',
        'A SHORT NAVIGATIONAL CTA TAKES THE MOTION VERB, NOT AN INVITATION, AND MUST NOT GROW. „Visit hub” (two words) is „Przejdź do centrum zasobów” or „Centrum zasobów”, never „Zapraszamy do centrum zasobów” — a five-word button is a layout risk as well as a register one. Reserve „Zapraszamy…” for one or two genuine invitations per page.',
        'WHEN TWO DIFFERENT ENGLISH LABELS SIT IN THE SAME MENU PANEL OR DROPDOWN, THEY MUST NOT COLLAPSE ONTO ONE POLISH WORD. „Training” is „Szkolenia” and „Training courses” is „Oferta szkoleń” (or „Kursy”) when both appear in one panel; the pack\'s de-pleonasm rule („Training courses” → „Szkolenia”) applies only when the other label is absent. Two identical sibling labels in one dropdown is a navigation defect, not a style choice.',
        'THE POLISH SKIP LINK IS „Przejdź do treści”, NEVER „Przejdź do zawartości”. „treść” is the settled Polish a11y/WCAG convention for page content; „zawartość” means the contents of a container. Screen-reader-only strings still follow market convention.',
        'DO NOT END A QUESTION OR CTA ON A BARE ADVERB OF TIME — POLISH LOSES THE URGENCY THERE. „Need support now?” is „Potrzebują Państwo wsparcia już teraz?” or „Potrzebują Państwo pomocy od ręki?”, not „…wsparcia teraz?”. Keep the modifier, but strengthen it to „już teraz” / „od ręki” and place it where it carries stress, and use ONE rendering of „now” across the whole page.',
        'COOKIE-CONSENT CATEGORY LABELS AGREE WITH THE IMPLIED PLURAL NOUN „pliki cookie”, SO THEY ARE ALL NON-MASCULINE PLURAL ADJECTIVES: „Ściśle konieczne”, „Funkcjonalne”, „Analityczne”, „Marketingowe” — never the masculine singular „Funkcjonalny” beside the plural „Ściśle konieczne”. One singular label in a set of plurals is a visible agreement error in the panel procurement and legal actually open.',
        'CONSENT-PANEL AND WIDGET CHROME IS BUYER-FACING TEXT AND MUST BE TRANSLATED, INCLUDING TABLE HEADERS, DURATIONS, DISCLOSURES, aria-labels AND input placeholders: „Name” → „Nazwa”, „Domain” → „Domena”, „Duration” → „Czas przechowywania”, „cookie”/„cookies” → „plik cookie”/„pliki cookie”, „Privacy Policy” → „Polityka prywatności” (matching the footer link), „Cookie consent” → „Zgoda na pliki cookie”, „Follow <Brand>” → „Obserwuj <Brand>”, „Search…” → „Szukaj…”. Never leave a full English sentence such as a data-processor disclosure inside an otherwise Polish EU consent UI.',
        'DURATIONS IN A COOKIE TABLE TAKE POLISH NUMERAL GOVERNMENT, NOT THE ENGLISH PATTERN: „2 lata”, „1 rok”, „3 miesiące”, „1 dzień”, „30 minut”, „10 minut”, „sesja”. Numerals 2–4 take the nominative plural and 5+ the genitive plural; a set of half-agreeing durations is a clear machine fingerprint.',
        'ENGLISH „utilities” IN A PLANT, CLIMATE OR ENERGY CONTEXT MEANS TECHNICAL MEDIA AND ENERGY INFRASTRUCTURE, NOT MUNICIPAL PUBLIC SERVICES. „utilities construction” is „budowa infrastruktury technicznej i energetycznej”, never „budowa infrastruktury użyteczności publicznej”, which reads as municipal works and hides the application from the industrial buyer it is aimed at.',
        'REUSE THE ALREADY-CORRECT POLISH STRING THAT EXISTS ELSEWHERE IN THE SAME DOCUMENT. When a sentence appears in more than one slot (meta description, og:description, JSON-LD „description”, title attribute, heading), emit ONE wording for all of them; never let a metadata field diverge from the structured-data copy of the same sentence.',
        'PREPOSITIONAL GOVERNMENT IN SET PHRASES IS NOT OPTIONAL, AND METADATA IS TEXT TOO. „z myślą o” takes the LOCATIVE: „z myślą o bezpieczeństwie, niezawodności i najwyższej wydajności” — never the accusative „z myślą o bezpieczeństwo, niezawodność i najwyższą wydajność”. When a preposition governs a coordinated list, every member of the list must carry that case, not just the first. Apply this with the same care to meta descriptions, og: tags, title attributes and JSON-LD as to body copy: those strings are the first Polish a buyer reads and a case error there is the most expensive one on the site.',
        'A BUTTON OR LINK LABEL MUST CONTAIN THE VERB OF THE ACTION THE BUYER TAKES. Never render an English imperative CTA as a bare noun phrase with a dangling adverbial: „Speak to an expert now” is „Porozmawiaj z ekspertem już teraz”, not „Rozmowa z ekspertem już teraz”; „Request a demo” is „Zamów demo”, not „Zapraszamy na demo” (which inverts the transaction — the company invites, the buyer attends); „Start a service ticket” is „Utwórz zgłoszenie serwisowe”. This supersedes the pack\'s older instruction to use impersonal noun phrases and „Zapraszamy…” for short CTAs: nominalised buttons systematically weaken every conversion point on the page. Keep Państwo in prose, questions and form instructions; use the imperative on the control itself.',
        'RESERVE „Prosimy + bezokolicznik” FOR ACTUAL INSTRUCTIONS, NOT FOR HEADINGS AND LABELS. A card heading or short label takes a Polish noun phrase („Zgłoszenie wsparcia”), a control takes a bare imperative („Prześlij zgłoszenie wsparcia”, „Szukaj”, „Zamknij”), and only a sentence that tells the buyer what to do in a form takes „Prosimy…”. An imperative sentence sitting in a title slot reads like a customs form.',
        '„Zapraszamy…” IS AN INVITATION AND MUST NOT BE THE DEFAULT FRAME FOR EVERY CTA ON A PAGE. Use it at most once or twice, for genuine invitations („Zapraszamy do grona partnerów wsparcia”); vary the rest with the verb the English uses. Five „Zapraszamy” CTAs on one page read as one translator\'s verbal habit rather than copywriting.',
        'READ-MORE LINKS ARE NOT ALL THE SAME STRING. Keep „Learn more” → „Więcej informacji”, but „Read more” / „Read article” / „Read announcement” on a news or press-release card take a verb and the right noun: „Czytaj więcej”, „Czytaj artykuł →”, „Czytaj komunikat →”. Never emit a bare fragment like „Całe ogłoszenie →”, and never use „ogłoszenie” for a press release — „ogłoszenie” is a classified ad or public notice; a press release is „komunikat (prasowy)”.',
        'USE ONE DASH CHARACTER FOR THE WHOLE SITE: the Polish półpauza „–” with spaces. Never emit the em dash „—”, not even when the English uses a hyphen or an em dash, and never let two dash characters appear across sibling entries of one menu or dropdown — mixed dashes across 19 parallel rows is a visible typography tell. (The pack already states this; enforce it on EVERY segment, including „Brand – opis” nav sub-lines.)',
        'IN A PRODUCTION CONTEXT „failure” IS „awaria”, NOT „niepowodzenie”. „niepowodzenie” is lack of success (a failed project or attempt); the cost a plant engineer cares about is the cost of a breakdown. Same test for „fault” → „usterka/wada”, „downtime” → „przestój”.',
        'STRIP ENGLISH FIRST-PERSON POSSESSIVES: Polish marks possession by inflection and context. „Ascential Care brings together our top technicians … to support our global customers. Our … platform …” becomes „Ascential Care łączy najlepszych techników … aby wspierać globalnych klientów. Platforma … ” — at most one „nasz” per paragraph, and none at all where the subject already owns the noun. Five „nasz/nasza/naszych” in two sentences is the single most recognisable translated-from-English tell.',
        'QUANTIFIERS PRECEDE POSSESSIVES IN POLISH: „wielu naszych marek”, „kilku naszych zakładów” — never the English order „naszych wielu marek”.',
        'CHECK THAT THE POLISH VERB COLLOCATES WITH THE NOUN BEFORE KEEPING THE ENGLISH PAIRING. „meet customer needs” is „zaspokajać potrzeby klientów” or „odpowiadać na potrzeby klientów” — „spełniać” collocates with oczekiwania, wymagania, marzenia, never with potrzeby. „unlock the performance / potential of your business” is „w pełni wykorzystać potencjał Państwa firmy” or „uwolnić potencjał…” — „odblokować” is what you do to a phone or a bank account.',
        'IDIOM-FOR-IDIOM ONLY WHEN THE SENSE MATCHES. English „a blank slate” in an engineering context means greenfield design: „zaczynając od zera” / „od podstaw”. „od czystej karty” in Polish means a reputational fresh start after past problems and is faintly unflattering in a capability claim. Before reusing a Polish idiom, check that its figurative sense is the English one, not merely its literal image.',
        'KEEP PARALLELISM IN COORDINATED VERBAL NOUNS AND KEEP EACH VERB\'S OWN SENSE. „collect, mine and measure data” is „gromadzenie, eksploracja i pomiar danych” — three nouns of the same type, and „mine” is data mining („eksploracja danych”), not „analizowanie”, which collides with the analytics pitch next to it.',
        'REPLACE ENGLISH LIST-CLOSERS INSTEAD OF CALQUING THEM: „and more” is „i nie tylko” or „i wiele innych <head noun>” — never the bare „i wiele więcej”, which is an English construction in Polish words.',
        'PLACE AN ADVERBIAL OF TIME WHERE IT CAN ONLY ATTACH TO THE VERB THE ENGLISH ATTACHES IT TO. Polish word order decides scope: „Zapraszamy do obejrzenia w ciągu kilku minut, jak integrujemy … system napędowy” (the watching takes minutes) vs „… w jeden system napędowy w ciągu kilku minut” (the integration takes minutes — an engineering claim the company is not making). When an English adverbial is ambiguous, pick the Polish position that makes the WEAKER, safer claim, never the stronger one.',
        'DO NOT DOWNGRADE „empowered” INTO PASSIVE CIRCUMSTANCE. „people are empowered to tackle …” is „ludzie zyskują siłę, by zmierzyć się z…” — „mają możliwość” („have the opportunity”) removes the company as the agent that confers the capability, i.e. removes it from its own mission statement. (This refines the older pack note that only banned „upoważnieni”.)',
        'PICK THE POLISH COLLOCATION, NOT THE WORD-BY-WORD RENDERING, IN STOCK MARKETING PHRASES: „the world moves forward” is „świat idzie naprzód” (never „postępuje naprzód”); „adapt swiftly” is „dostosowywać się szybko” (never the vaguer „dynamicznie”); „responsiveness” is „krótki czas reakcji”; „with low operational impact” is „o niewielkim wpływie na eksploatację”, never the calque „o niskim wpływie operacyjnym”.',
        'OPTIONS IN ONE DROPDOWN MUST BE MUTUALLY DISTINGUISHABLE, EVEN WHEN TWO ENGLISH LABELS OVERLAP. If one option names a division („Aerospace & Industrials | …”) and another names a narrower brand scope („Bauer | Aerospace”), the Polish must keep them different („Lotnictwo i przemysł | …” vs „Bauer | Lotnictwo”). Two identical labels on options that route to different teams is a functional defect in the support path, not a style issue — it outweighs the one-term-per-segment rule, which applies only when the English really names the same unit.',
        'A CORPORATE RANK NEVER CHANGES TIER IN TRANSLATION, AND ONE ENGLISH RANK MAPS TO ONE POLISH RANK SITEWIDE: Director = „dyrektor” (Regional Director = „dyrektor regionalny”), Manager = „kierownik”, General Manager = „dyrektor generalny (zakładu)”. „kierownik” for a Director demotes a named executive a rung and inverts the org chart against other cards in the same news grid.',
        'USE THE SHORT MODERN POLISH FORM THE TRADE AND THE MARKET ACTUALLY WRITE: „eBooks” → „E-booki” (never „Książki elektroniczne”), „Terms” → „Warunki korzystania” (bare „Warunki” is too thin for a legal footer link), „Corporate information” → „Informacje o firmie” in nav AND footer (never „Informacje korporacyjne”). Lock one Polish label per recurring English label and reuse it wherever that label appears.',
        'DROP REDUNDANT POSSESSIVES AND USE THE PROPER ELLIPSIS IN PLACEHOLDERS: „Type your message...” is „Wpisz wiadomość…” — no „swoją”, and the single character „…” (U+2026), never three ASCII dots, so every placeholder on the page matches.',
        'DISAMBIGUATE A SHOP-FLOOR NOUN THAT HAS A STREET MEANING. In a location hint, „column” is „słup konstrukcyjny” (bare „słup” reads as a utility pole); „cell” is „gniazdo produkcyjne”; „line” is „linia (produkcyjna)”. Add the qualifying word rather than leaving the bare noun to be misread.',
        'WHERE AN ENGLISH DEVICE DOUBLET NAMES TWO REAL INPUT METHODS THE BUYER USES, KEEP BOTH: „Tap or click here” is „Prosimy dotknąć lub kliknąć tutaj” — on a phone there is nothing to click. (This supersedes the older pack instruction to collapse tap/click to „Prosimy kliknąć tutaj”.) Collapse a doublet only when the second branch adds no method the reader could actually use.',
        'SHOP-FLOOR VOCABULARY: a manufacturing cell is „gniazdo produkcyjne”, never „komórka” (which means a biological cell, a mobile phone or an org unit). A structural column on a plant floor is „słup”, not „kolumna”. „machine health” is „stan techniczny (maszyn)”, never „kondycja maszyn” — kondycja belongs to fitness and finance. „gauging” (dimensional checking) is „kontrola wymiarowa”, never bare „pomiary”, which collides with „pomiary NVH” in the same list.',
        'EFFECTIVE vs EFFICIENT IS A FALSE-FRIEND PAIR IN POLISH. „effective” (achieves its purpose) is „skuteczny”; „efektywny” means resource-efficient and is the classic EN→PL slip. Same test for „efficiency” → „efektywność / wydajność” only when the English really means economy of resources.',
        'WHITEPAPER IS NOT „biała księga”. In Polish „biała księga” denotes a government or EU policy paper; a commercial technical download is „raport techniczny” (plural „Raporty techniczne”), or the borrowed „whitepaper”. Use the same Polish label for the category list item and for every individual asset title, so „Whitepapers” and „… Whitepaper” never diverge.',
        'DO NOT COORDINATE A BARE NOUN PHRASE WITH A FINITE CLAUSE USING „lub” or „i”. English „Machine down or need a hand?” cannot become „Awaria maszyny lub potrzebują Państwo pomocy?”. Split it into two questions — „Awaria maszyny? A może potrzebują Państwo pomocy?” — or give both branches the same syntactic shape. Same rule for „X and field/remote service”: write „serwis terenowy i zdalny”, not „serwis w terenie i zdalny”.',
        'A PRONOUN MUST AGREE WITH THE NOUN IT REPLACES, NOT WITH THE SITUATION. After „zgłoszenie serwisowe” write „zajmie się nim”, not the vague „zajmie się tym”. Trace the antecedent before choosing the pronoun.',
        'GIVE EACH ENGLISH SUPPORT NOUN ITS OWN POLISH NOUN INSIDE A FORM: request = „zgłoszenie”, case = „sprawa”, ticket = „zgłoszenie serwisowe”. Never let two of them collapse onto one word in consecutive sentences the buyer has to fill in — „Jakiego rodzaju jest to sprawa? Czy mogą Państwo opisać swoje zgłoszenie bardziej szczegółowo?”',
        'ONE POLISH NAME PER BUSINESS SEGMENT ACROSS NAV, FOOTER AND EVERY DROPDOWN OPTION. „Aerospace & industrials” and the bare „Aerospace” that names the same unit must both render as „Lotnictwo i przemysł” — including in „Brand | Segment” option labels such as „Bauer | Lotnictwo i przemysł”. Two labels for one unit on one page makes the buyer guess whether they are the same team. (This supersedes the older instruction to render „Bauer | Aerospace” as „Bauer | Lotnictwo i kosmonautyka”.)',
        '„Tap or click here” IS ONE ACTION IN POLISH: „Prosimy kliknąć tutaj”. Do not calque „tap” as „dotknąć”. Generally, collapse English device-hedging doublets (tap/click, call or text) to the single verb Polish sites actually use.',
        'FORM FIELD LABELS ARE POLISH NOUN PHRASES, NOT CALQUED ENGLISH HEADS. „Contact name” is „Osoba kontaktowa” (not „Imię i nazwisko kontaktu”); „Attach files (optional)” is „Załączniki (opcjonalnie)”. A noun label also keeps the label out of the ty/Państwo register question entirely — prefer it over any imperative inside a Państwo form.',
        'POLISH VERBS DO NOT TAKE „możliwości” AS AN OBJECT OF DESIGN. „we engineer new … possibilities” is „tworzymy nowe możliwości”, never „projektujemy możliwości” (one designs systems, machines, processes). When English uses an abstract noun as the object of a concrete verb, swap the verb, and move a long adjective string after the noun with a półpauza: „tworzymy nowe możliwości – szybkie, precyzyjne i bezkompromisowe”.',
        'ADD NO INTENSIFIER THE ENGLISH LACKS IN TIME SPANS. „in a few minutes” is „w ciągu kilku minut”; reserve „zaledwie” for an English „just / only / in as little as”. (The earlier pack note about „w ciągu zaledwie kilku minut” was about case government — „w ciągu + dopełniacz”, not „w zaledwie kilka minut” — and does not license adding „zaledwie”.)',
        'STACKED „na” IS A CLUNK. „<rank>, Americas” after „na stanowisku” becomes „na stanowisku kierownika serwisu dla regionu obu Ameryk”, not „na stanowisku … na region obu Ameryk”. Avoid repeating the same preposition twice in one appointment headline; vary to „dla regionu…”, „w segmencie…”, „ds. …”.',
        'USE THE TRADE ABBREVIATION WHERE THE TRADE USES IT. „service level agreements” is „umowy SLA”, not the heavy „umowy dotyczące poziomów usług”, in nav sub-lines, cards and buttons. Expand only where the source itself spells the term out for a lay reader.',
        'APOSTROPHES AND QUOTES ARE TYPOGRAPHIC EVERYWHERE, IN EVERY SEGMENT. A declined foreign surname uses U+2019: „Kime’a”, „Michalet’a”-pattern names, „Nate’a”, „Jerome’a” — never the straight ASCII \'. The same source name rendered with ’ in one segment and \' in another on the same page is a visible machine-translation tell.',
        'LOCK ONE POLISH VERB PER ENGLISH PRESS-RELEASE VERB ACROSS THE WHOLE NEWS FEED: Announces = „ogłasza powołanie … na stanowisko”, Appoints = „powołuje … na stanowisko”, Hires = „zatrudnia … na stanowisko”, Promotes = „awansuje … na stanowisko”, Welcomes = „wita … na stanowisku”. Do not let „powołuje” absorb three different English verbs; the mapping must be systematic across every card.',
        'ASPECT CARRIES MEANING: an ongoing capability takes the IMPERFECTIVE. „allowing us to adapt” is „pozwalając nam dostosowywać się”, not the perfective „dostosować się”, which names a single completed adjustment.',
        'A COORDINATED PRE-MODIFIER LIST IS N PRODUCTS, NOT ONE. \'Chassis, hub & steerable dyno\' names three dynamometers: \'Hamownie podwoziowe, piastowe i do kół skrętnych\'. Never resolve the serial comma into a feature chain (\'Hamownia podwoziowa z piastą i kołami skrętnymi\'), which silently deletes two products from the catalogue. Pluralise the shared head noun and give every modifier its own agreeing form.',
        '\'DOWN\' IN AN EQUIPMENT CONTEXT IS A BREAKDOWN, NOT A SWITCH POSITION. \'Machine down\' = \'Awaria maszyny\'; \'the machine or system is down\' = \'maszyna lub system jest unieruchomiony\'. \'wyłączona/wyłączony\' means deliberately switched off and destroys the urgency that justifies a service CTA.',
        'PROCESS AND MASS NOUNS DO NOT PLURALISE. \'precision machining\' is \'precyzyjna obróbka skrawaniem\', never \'precyzyjne obróbki\'. Nouns in -anie, -enie and -óbka naming a process stay singular however the English is phrased.',
        'A CUSTOMER\'S \'request\' IS \'zgłoszenie\', NEVER \'żądanie\'. \'żądanie\' is a demand or legal claim; telling your own customers they issue demands is a tonal miss. Keep one noun for it across the whole form and the whole site.',
        'POLISH DOES NOT STACK BARE NOUNS AS MODIFIERS. \'Burke Porter automotive\' is \'Burke Porter – motoryzacja\'; \'Burke Porter ADAS systems\' is \'Systemy ADAS Burke Porter\'. Either put the brand after the Polish head noun or separate it with a dash — never copy English noun-noun order.',
        'DO NOT REPEAT THE ROOT OF A MACHINE\'S NAME IN ITS FUNCTION. \'Wyważarka CMT-TR do wyważania rdzeni\' is tautological — write \'Wyważarka niskoobrotowa CMT-TR do rdzeni\'. Fold English redundancy out rather than transposing it.',
        'TRANSLATE EVERY OPTION IN A PARALLEL SET. If \'Transportation | Burke Porter\' becomes \'Transport | Burke Porter\', then \'Bauer | Aerospace\' must become \'Bauer | Lotnictwo i kosmonautyka\'. One untranslated sibling in a dropdown is more obviously machine-generated than translating none of them.',
        'A MODIFIER MUST LAND ON A NOUN. \'other diverse industries\' cannot end as the dangling \'i innych zróżnicowanych\' — write \'oraz wielu innych zróżnicowanych branż\'. If preserving a modifier leaves an adjective stranded, supply the head noun the Polish sentence needs.',
        'SUPERLATIVES AND MARKET LISTS ARE LOAD-BEARING. \'the world\'s most innovative companies\' is \'najbardziej innowacyjnych firm na świecie\' — \'światowych innowacyjnych firm\' both drops \'most\' and is not idiomatic. \'the transportation, medical and life sciences, and industrial markets\' is THREE markets: \'na rynkach transportu, medycyny i nauk przyrodniczych oraz przemysłu\' — do not split \'medical and life sciences\' into two, which inflates the served-market count.',
        'KEEP CLAIM BREADTH IN PERFORMANCE WORDS. \'excel in performance\' is \'wyróżniać się osiągami\'; \'wydajność\' means throughput/efficiency and narrows the promise.',
        'PREPOSITION GOVERNMENT IS NOT COPIED FROM ENGLISH. \'diagnostics across your production equipment\' is \'diagnostyka w całym parku maszynowym\' — \'na sprzęcie\' means physically on top of it. Check which Polish preposition the verb or noun actually takes before rendering across / for / with.',
        'NUMERAL GOVERNMENT IS MANDATORY IN STAT COUNTERS. Polish numerals of 5 and above, and any \'<number>+\' quantity, govern the GENITIVE PLURAL. Write \'2300+ ekspertów\', \'40+ lokalizacji na całym świecie\', \'70+ lat innowacji\', \'20+ krajów macierzystych\' — never the nominative \'Eksperci\', \'lokalizacje\'. When a UI string arrives as the bare label only (\'expert people\', \'global locations\'), assume a numeral precedes it and emit the genitive plural anyway; half-right agreement across a set of counters is the clearest machine-translation fingerprint.',
        'MATCH THE CAPITALISATION OF SIBLING LABELS. In a set of parallel counter labels, nav items or bullets, every item must share one capitalisation pattern. \'Eksperci\' capitalised beside lowercase \'lat innowacji\' and \'krajów macierzystych\' reads as a separately machine-translated segment.',
        'NEVER LEAVE A SERVICE DESCRIPTION IN ENGLISH BECAUSE IT CONTAINS AN ACRONYM. \'NDT inspection\' is not a brand; translate it and keep the acronym in parentheses: \'badania nieniszczące (NDT)\'. The untranslated-brand allowance covers only registered names (Ascential, Ascential Care, Ascentialytics, Sentia, Cimat, Galileo, Kleinknecht, Lismar, Titan, Burke Porter, WinterPark, XL Machine, Bauer). One English descriptor sitting among Polish siblings in a dropdown is the single most visible defect a reviewer can find.',
        'ONE POLISH TERM PER CONCEPT ACROSS THE WHOLE SITE. Reviewers found NDT rendered three ways on one page (\'NDT inspection\' / \'kontrola nieniszczące\' / \'Badania nieniszczące\') and the resources hub four ways (\'Centrum zasobów\' / \'hub zasobów\' / \'Odwiedź hub\' / \'Hub aplikacji i zasobów\'). Before emitting a recurring term, reuse the form already used in the nav: badania nieniszczące, Centrum zasobów, branża metalurgiczna, Marketplace części zamiennych, zgłoszenie.',
        'A MULTI-WORD BRAND IS NEVER TRANSLATED AND NEVER TRUNCATED. \'XL Machine\' stays \'XL Machine\' — not \'Maszyna XL\' (a common noun) and not \'XL\' (truncated inside a coordinated list). \'ADAS Garage\' stays \'ADAS Garage\' because the page links it to youtube.com/@ADASGarage. If a brand looks like an ordinary noun phrase, that is exactly when it must be left alone.',
        'CORPORATE RANKS ARE DISTINCT TIERS AND MAP ONE-TO-ONE. Executive Vice President = \'wiceprezes wykonawczy\' (feminine: \'wiceprezes wykonawcza\'), Senior Vice President = \'starszy wiceprezes\', Vice President = \'wiceprezes\'. Never let two different English ranks collapse onto one Polish title on the same site — in an appointment announcement that is a factual error about a named person.',
        'DO NOT MOVE A MODIFIER FROM THE PRODUCT ONTO THE READER, AND DO NOT ADD A CLAIM. In \'Real-time remote monitoring for your production equipment\', \'remote\' describes the monitoring, not the user\'s location: \'Zdalne monitorowanie parku maszynowego w czasie rzeczywistym\'. Never invent \'z dowolnego miejsca\', and never broaden the object (\'park maszynowy\') to the vaguer \'produkcja\'.',
        'CHECK WHETHER THE POLISH ADJECTIVE CARRIES A FOREIGN DOMAIN SENSE. \'field service/support\' is \'serwis w terenie\' or \'serwis terenowy\' — \'polowy\' is military (kuchnia polowa). Same test for \'zasób\' (accounting) where an engineer expects \'urządzenie\', and \'rynek\' (a sector) where the source means a storefront (\'Marketplace\'/\'Giełda\').',
        'NEVER INVENT A POLISH WORD BY BOLTING A POLISH ENDING ONTO AN ENGLISH STEM. \'nieurgentny\' does not exist — write \'niepilny\'. If a negated or Latinate adjective is not one you can attest in Polish usage, use the native equivalent: niepilny, zapobiegawczy (not profilaktyczny for preventive maintenance), wykrywanie (not detekcja).',
        'EVERY BRANCH OF A SLASH OR ALTERNATIVE PAIR AGREES WITH THE SHARED HEAD NOUN. \'Priorytet 3: Niski priorytet / Rutynowy\' — \'Rutynowe\' has nothing to agree with. Trace the head noun before inflecting the second element of any \'X / Y\' label.',
        'USE THE TERM THE TRADE PRINTS IN CATALOGUES, NOT THE GENERAL-LANGUAGE LOOK-ALIKE. A mill roll is \'walec\' (never \'rolka\', a small roller); a roll shop is \'szlifiernia walców\' (never \'warsztat walcarni\'); actuation is \'układy wykonawcze / siłowniki\' (never \'systemy sterowania\', which is control systems — a different rig and a different buyer); air handling units are \'centrale wentylacyjne\'; end-of-line automation is \'automatyzacja końca linii produkcyjnej\' and covers assembly, marking and handling as well as test, so never narrow it to \'testów końcowych\'.',
        'KEEP ASSET-TYPE CATEGORIES DISTINCT WHEN THE SITE LISTS THEM SIDE BY SIDE. If \'Reports\' already exists as its own category, \'Whitepapers\' must be \'Białe księgi\', not \'Raporty\'. Never merge two labelled content types into one Polish word.',
        'DROP THE ENGLISH CATEGORY WORD WHEN THE POLISH NOUN ALREADY CONTAINS IT. \'Training courses\' is \'Szkolenia\', not \'Kursy szkoleniowe\' (a pleonasm). Same for \'usługi serwisowe serwisu\' and similar doubled heads.',
        'ENGLISH APPOSITIVE COMMAS AFTER A JOB TITLE DO NOT EXIST IN POLISH, AND AMERICAN TITLE PATTERNS NEED A POLISH EQUIVALENT. \'Service Manager, Americas\' = \'kierownik serwisu na region obu Ameryk\'; \'General Manager of X Location\' = \'dyrektor zakładu w X\', never \'kierownik generalny lokalizacji\'. \'the Americas\' is plural: \'obie Ameryki\', \'w obu Amerykach\' — never \'Ameryka\' / \'w Ameryce\'. \'Welcomes X\' is \'wita X\', not \'przyjmuje\' (accepts/takes in).',
        'EMIT ONLY FORMS THAT EXIST IN THE PARADIGM. Surnames in -a decline like feminine nouns: Herrera -> Herrerę (acc.), Herrery (gen.); \'Herrere\' is not a form. Names ending in a pronounced consonant take no apostrophe: Drew -> Drewa, not Drew\'a. If you are unsure of the paradigm, leave the name undeclined rather than inventing an ending.',
        'REGISTER — THE SITE IS Państwo, INCLUDING EVERY CTA, BUTTON, FIELD LABEL AND HEADLINE. This overrides the CTA glossary entries and examples elsewhere in this pack: do NOT emit \'Dowiedz się więcej\', \'Umów demo\', \'Przeczytaj artykuł\', \'Zobacz\', \'Wybierz\', \'Skontaktuj się\', \'Zostań\', \'Przewiduj\', \'Obejrzyj\', \'Twój/Twoja\'. Use instead (a) an impersonal noun phrase for short CTAs — \'Więcej informacji\', \'Cały artykuł\', \'Wszystkie komunikaty prasowe\', \'Rozmowa z ekspertem już teraz\', \'Nowe zgłoszenie serwisowe\'; (b) \'Prosimy + bezokolicznik\' for form instructions — \'Prosimy wybrać zespół wsparcia\', \'Prosimy opisać zgłoszenie\'; (c) \'Zapraszamy…\' for invitations — \'Zapraszamy na demo\', \'Zapraszamy do centrum zasobów\'; (d) third-person plural with Państwo for questions and statements — \'Czy potrzebują Państwo pomocy w czymś innym?\', \'Mogą Państwo do nas zadzwonić\'. Bare imperatives remain acceptable only for controls acting on the interface itself (Zamknij, Zapisz, Wyślij, Szukaj).',
        'SECOND-PERSON PLURAL (wy) IS NEVER POLITE IN POLISH, WITH OR WITHOUT Państwo. \'Zobaczcie\', \'Skontaktujcie się\', \'Możecie Państwo\' are all wrong. Write \'Tak łączymy to wszystko w całość\' or \'Zobaczą Państwo…\', \'Prosimy o kontakt\', \'Mogą Państwo\'. Equally, never pair a singular verb with Państwo: \'Potrzebujesz Państwo\', \'Czy może Państwo\' -> \'Czy potrzebują Państwo\', \'Czy mogą Państwo\'.',
        'WHEN ONE HEADING IS SPLIT ACROSS SEVERAL SEGMENTS OR SPANS, TRANSLATE IT AS ONE SENTENCE AND KEEP EVERY FRAGMENT MUTUALLY CONSISTENT. \'See how we bring it all\' + \'together\' and the full \'See how we bring it all together\' must produce the same Polish wording; two different renderings of one source heading on one page is a visible MT tell.',
        'ANNOUNCEMENT HEADLINES: awansować / mianować / powołać / zatrudnić take "na stanowisko" (accusative), never "na stanowisku". "Ascential ogłasza Raymonda Kime\'a na stanowisku..." is wrong; write "Ascential powołuje Raymonda Kime\'a na stanowisko..." or "...ogłasza powołanie Raymonda Kime\'a na stanowisko...". Reviewers found this error 14 times across the news feed.',
        'WORD ORDER in "complex, mission-critical products and solutions": "złożone produkty i rozwiązania o kluczowym znaczeniu". Never "złożonych, krytycznych dla misji produktów".',
        '"low-bearing" / "high-bearing" balancing machines are low-speed / high-speed ("niskoobrotowe" / "wysokoobrotowe"). "niskoosiowych" and "wysokoosiowych" are not Polish words.',
        '"timely insights" keeps the time claim: "wnioski we właściwym czasie" or "wnioski na czas". Do not replace it with "praktyczne" (actionable), which is a different promise.',
        '"turbo balancing" and "turbocharger" are "turbosprężarka", never "turbina" (turbine), which is a different machine for a different buyer.',
        'PAŃSTWO TAKES THIRD-PERSON PLURAL, NEVER SECOND. \'Możecie Państwo\' and \'Czy możecie\' are the single clearest non-native markers in Polish B2B copy. Write \'Mogą Państwo zadzwonić\', \'Czy mogą Państwo udostępnić\'. Never \'możecie\', \'jesteście\', \'chcecie\' with Państwo.',
        'ONE REGISTER PER DOCUMENT, AND NEVER TWO IN ONE SENTENCE. Reviewers found \'Dowiedz się, ... mogą pomóc Państwu\' — an informal imperative and a formal pronoun in the same clause. That is the signature of segment-by-segment machine translation. Commit to Państwo everywhere: \'Potrzebują Państwo pomocy?\' not \'Potrzebujesz pomocy?\'; \'Prosimy o kontakt\' not \'Skontaktuj się\'; \'Prosimy opisać\' not \'Opisz\'; \'Dowiedzą się Państwo\' not \'Dowiedz się\'.',
        'ADJECTIVE MUST AGREE WITH ITS NOUN IN CASE. \'bystrych umysły\' mixes genitive adjective with accusative noun — impossible for a native. Also avoid the calque itself: \'sharp minds\' is \'wiedza ekspercka\' or \'doświadczeni specjaliści\' in capital-equipment copy, never \'bystre umysły\', which reads juvenile.',
        'ABSTRACT NOUNS CANNOT TAKE HUMAN ADJECTIVES. \'nieustępliwe możliwości\' is impossible: nieustępliwy describes a person who will not back down. For uncompromising capability write \'bezkompromisowe rozwiązania\'. Check every adjective against whether its noun is animate.',
        'VERB GOVERNMENT: kierować takes the instrumental (kieruje nami cel), NOT the accusative. \'kieruje nas cel\' is ungrammatical. napędzać in the sense of motivating takes an accusative OBJECT with a third-person verb: \'Napędza nas wiedza\', never \'Napędzamy nas\' which means \'we drive us\'.',
        'POLISH QUESTION WORD ORDER, not transplanted English. \'Jaki typ żądania to jest?\' is English word order in Polish words. Write \'Jakiego typu jest to zgłoszenie?\' or better \'Czego dotyczy zgłoszenie?\'. Prefer a natural Polish question to a literal rendering of the English one.',
        'REGISTER: use Państwo consistently in every sentence that addresses the reader. Never mix it with ty-imperatives. \'Przewiduj awarie\' and \'Potrzebujesz pomocy?\' are wrong here — write \'Proszę przewidywać awarie\' / \'Czy potrzebują Państwo pomocy?\' or recast impersonally.',
        'JOB TITLES are lowercase in Polish, never English Title Case. \'wiceprezes ds. globalnych operacji produkcyjnych\', NOT \'Wiceprezesa ds. Globalnych Operacji Produkcyjnych\'. Keep every rank word: SVP is \'starszy wiceprezes\', do not drop \'Senior\'.',
        'APPOINTMENT ANNOUNCEMENTS: do not calque \'announces X as\'. Write \'X obejmuje stanowisko...\' or \'...ogłasza nominację X na stanowisko...\'. The verb awansować na takes the ACCUSATIVE: \'awansuje Brunna Morettiego na stanowisko\', not \'na stanowisku\'.',
        'MALE SURNAMES ending in -o decline as masculine: Brunno -> Brunna, not Brunnę (that is feminine). Names pronounced as written take no apostrophe before a Polish ending: Jaya, not Jay\'a.',
        'COMMA before a subordinate conjunction is obligatory: \'awarie, zanim wystąpią\', \'Esc, aby zamknąć\'. English omits it; Polish does not.',
        'TERMINOLOGY the industrial audience actually uses: dynamometer = hamownia (hamownia podwoziowa), NOT dynamometr. end-of-line automation = automatyka testów końcowych (EOL), not a word-for-word calque. insights = wnioski, not wglądy. mission-critical = o kluczowym znaczeniu, not krytyczne dla misji. unsubscribe = Wypisz się, not Zrezygnuj. Imprint = Nota prawna. landing gear = podwozie alone (podwozie lotnicze if disambiguation is needed); \'podwozia lądowania\' is redundant.',
        'EMPOWERED is not upoważnieni (that means legally authorised). Use \'mają możliwość\', \'są w stanie\' or recast. RELENTLESS is not bezwzględny (ruthless): use \'niestrudzony\' or \'konsekwentny\'.',
        'AGREEMENT: check every adjective against its noun. \'Nasze wyniki\' not \'Nasz wyniki\'; \'zaawansowany montaż\' not \'zaawansowane montaż\'. Check every verb against its subject: \'napędza nas doświadczenie\' not \'napędzamy nas doświadczenie\'.',
        'TIME SPANS: \'w ciągu zaledwie kilku minut\', not \'w zaledwie kilka minut\'.',
        'ONE NAME PER SERVICE across the whole site. Pick \'Wyważanie jako usługa (BaaS)\' and use it every time; never alternate with \'Wyważanie kontraktowe jako usługa\'.',
        'In inflected languages, check that every noun and its modifiers carry the case, gender and number demanded by the governing preposition or verb; a dictionary-form phrase left mid-sentence is the clearest machine-translation tell.',
        'When inserting a multi-word industry, sector or product-category name into a sentence, translate and decline the entire phrase to agree with its head noun — never paste a glossary entry in citation form.',
        'Never render \'solve a challenge\' as \'rozwiązać wyzwanie\'; write \'sprostać wyzwaniu\' or recast the noun as \'problem\'.',
        'Add no qualifier the English lacks: \'under pressure\' is \'pod presją\' or \'w warunkach presji\', never \'pod presją czasu\'.',
        'Preserve the force of source participles: \'focused on\' is \'skupionych na\' or \'zaangażowanych w\', not \'zainteresowanych\'.',
        'Keep role nouns at source specificity: \'technicians\' is \'technicy\', not the broader \'specjaliści\'.',
        'Keep \'working toward a master\'s degree\' as ongoing enrolment (\'studiuje na studiach magisterskich\'); never imply completion or near-graduation.',
        'Maintain the Państwo register in every address to the reader; never drop to ty-forms or bare second-person imperatives.',
        'FIDELITY: \'working toward\' (in progress, no stated stage) became \'kończy\' = \'is finishing/completing\'. The Polish asserts he is near graduation — a factual claim about a named person\'s credentials that the English does not make. RO (\'urmează un master\') and CS (\'studuje magisterský program\') render it correctly, confirming the Polish is the outlier.',
        'Lock one courtesy register before translating and hold it in every single string, including two-word CTAs, headlines, questions and imperatives: formal Państwo forms only, never second-person singular (Masz, Zapytaj, Twój, możesz). Short marketing strings are where the register silently breaks.',
        'Never translate an English verb+noun pair word for word — verify the Polish verb actually governs that noun. Wyzwaniu się sprosta lub stawia czoła (nigdy „rozwiązać wyzwanie”, „pomóc w wyzwaniu”); rozwiązuje się problem; projektuje się systemy, nie możliwości; w życie wciela się pomysły, nie pytania.',
        'Insert a non-breaking space (U+00A0) after every one-letter word — w, z, i, o, u, a, e — in every string without exception. This is mandatory Polish typography, not a stylistic choice, and applies to headings, bullets and alt text as well as body copy.',
        'Before finalising a sentence, trace every pronoun to its real antecedent and check that each verb object can literally undergo the action; if it cannot, rewrite the clause instead of preserving the English structure.',
        'When English pairs a generic category with a specific one (Aerospace or Industrial, business and enterprise), give each branch its own distinct Polish noun or adjective; never let the same head noun appear twice, which reads as an untranslated placeholder.',
        'Keep parallel list items syntactically and punctuationally identical: same construction, same head noun, and a comma before apposition markers such as „takich jak” in every item, not only in some of them.',
        'In technical enumerations every listed item must belong to the category named by the head noun — list „wirniki pomp” among rotors, never „pompy”. Mixing components with whole machines instantly marks the text as written by a non-specialist.',
        'Replace vague English quantifiers and list-closers instead of calquing them: \'a wide range of\' → „wiele rodzajów” / „różne” (keep „szeroka gama” only for product ranges), \'and more\' → „i wiele innych” or drop it.',
        'Pick one courtesy register and hold it across every string on the site: use formal Państwo forms in all questions, CTAs and imperatives, and never switch to second-person singular (Masz, Zapytaj, Twój).',
        'Do not carry an abstract English noun across literally when the bare Polish noun says nothing to a business reader; expand it into the collocation a Polish specialist uses (proximity → "bliski kontakt z klientem", not "bliskość").',
        'Never pair a Polish verb with an English object that does not collocate: not "rozwiązać wyzwanie" (→ sprostać wyzwaniu / rozwiązać problem), not "pomóc w wyzwaniu" (→ pomóc rozwiązać wyzwanie).',
        'Delete possessive pronouns (nasz, nasza, naszych, swoich) wherever ownership is already obvious; Polish marks possession far more sparingly than English — aim for at most one "nasz" per paragraph.',
        'Render English "built/designed for X and Y" with an explicit Polish preposition for each element (do pracy w… i przy…); never chain unlike nouns under a single "dla".',
        'Keep web copy out of officialese and literary archaism: prefer "ma/uzyskał/ukończył" over "posiada", "sprawić, by" over "czynić", and finite clauses over stacked participles such as "uzyskany w…".',
        'Insert a non-breaking space after every one-letter word (w, z, i, o, u, a) so it can never end a line, and apply enumeration punctuation identically across parallel bullets (comma before "takich jak" in all of them or none).',
        'Use the established Polish specialist term rather than a word-for-word rendering (systemy kontrolno-pomiarowe, prądy wirowe, czopy, wyważarki pionowe/poziome), and reserve "szeroka gama" for product ranges only.',
        'Use „…” (U+201E and U+201D) as the only quotation marks in Polish text; never close a quotation with a straight " or an English closing mark, and never mix the two within one string.',
        'Keep one honorific register across the entire site: address the reader as Państwo (Mają Państwo…, proszę…) and never slip into second-person singular (masz, zapytaj, sprawdź, poznaj), including in short CTAs, buttons and headlines.',
        'Decline foreign product, brand and personal names according to Polish case when grammar demands it (Zapytaj Sentię, korzystając z Ascentialytics); leave a name undeclined only when it is a fixed alphanumeric code.',
