        'Never calque the English purpose pattern \'for + noun\'. Use an adjectival participle (zapewniający, umożliwiający, pozwalający na) or \'w celu + rzeczownik odsłowny\'.',
        'Prefer the native Polish noun over the Latinate look-alike when one exists: detection → wykrywanie (not detekcja), defect → wada (not defekt), inspection → kontrola/badanie (not inspekcja), monitoring → monitorowanie.',
        'Render English marketing verbs idiomatically, not literally: \'Powered by\' → \'Oparte na / Wykorzystujące\' (never \'Napędzane\'); \'deep expertise\' → \'dogłębna wiedza / rozległe doświadczenie\' (never \'głęboka wiedza\'); \'connected solution\' → \'zintegrowane rozwiązanie\'.',
        'Verify every technical compound against real Polish trade usage instead of translating word by word: paper mill → maszyna papiernicza/papiernia (not walcarka), electrical industry → przemysł elektrotechniczny, robotics hardware → roboty/systemy robotyczne (not robotyka).',
        'Fix source redundancy rather than transposing it, and lock one Polish equivalent per recurring term for the whole site (e.g. test and measurement → systemy kontrolno-pomiarowe / badania i pomiary) — never alternate variants between items.',
        'Use Polish quotation marks „…" not English "…".',
        'Capitalize only the first word of headlines and sentences. Never carry over English title case.',
        'Capitalize months and days only at the start of a sentence (not mid-sentence).',
        'Use a non-breaking space after single-letter prepositions (w, z, o, i, a, u) to prevent them from ending a line. Emit the actual Unicode non-breaking space character (U+00A0) — do NOT emit the HTML entity &nbsp; or &NBSP;, because some WordPress contexts double-escape it and it renders as literal text on the page.',
        'Decline company-name dependents correctly: "z firmą Acme" (instrumental), not "z firma Acme".',
